# marketing/ renders. animate_logo.py regenerates every one of these from
# fusenest.svg, which is the only input: `preview` writes fusenest_anim.svg and
# preview.html, `video --out <file>` encodes each of the four. Sources are
# tracked; renders are not. The .mov alone is 196MB of ProRes, and a render
# committed once stays in the history for good.
marketing/fusenest_anim.svg
marketing/preview.html
marketing/fusenest_logo.*
marketing/frames/
marketing/venv/
